Only resolve the Go SDK to a path in `compute_env` when `go` is actually run.

`compute_env` (used by `bazel_gazelle_go_repository_cache` and the `go_deps` extension) called
`ctx.path()` on the SDK's `ROOT` label unconditionally, but the result is only needed for the
`GO_REPOSITORY_USE_HOST_{MOD,}CACHE` branches; `GOROOT` is recorded as a label. With
`--experimental_remote_repo_contents_cache`, `ctx.path(Label)` materialises the whole SDK, and
the non-reproducible `bazel_gazelle_go_repository_cache` runs on every fresh server because each
`go_repository` records its `go.env` as an input. Consumers that run `go` (`go_repository_tools`,
`go_repository` on a cache miss) still resolve the label via `read_go_env_file`.

Not yet raised upstream.

